  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "The three senses are often three different expressions in other languages: one for nevertheless, one for besides or in any case, and a spoken marker for moving on. Do not translate them with one word.",
    "grammar": "The position matters: at the end of the clause anyway means despite that; at the start it adds a reason or changes the subject.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "Three syllables with the stress on the first: EN-ee-way. The first vowel is the short e of pen."
